      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please go to urgent care or the ER right away. A deep, rusted cut with spreading redness, warmth, and throbbing is a classic sign of a serious bacterial infection that can quickly turn into cellulitis or tetanus—and warm compresses and honey won't be enough to stop that. Antibiotics are necessary here, and your preference to avoid them isn't worth the risk of the infection spreading to your bloodstream. This is not something to treat at home; a doctor can also assess if you need a tetanus shot.",
